# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale ro
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as [12:00, 18:00).
# The hyphenated surface is tokenizer-canonicalised to "dupa amiaza" (the
# hyphen splits into two tokens the loader re-glues) -- the same reason
# fr's daypart_apres_midi_fr.voc keeps this comment. Registering it here is
# required because bare "amiaza" is ALSO this locale's word for noon
# (clock_landmark_720.voc): without the glued multi-token surface, the
# hyphen-split "amiaza" half of "dupa-amiaza" was claimed by the noon
# landmark instead of the afternoon band.
după-amiaza
dupa-amiaza
după-amiază
